<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- App-host Activity theme for the C++ MAUI gallery on Android. Shared by BOTH hosts: the C++ builder
     host (AndroidManifest.xml beside this file) and the C++&XAML host
     (examples/gallery_xaml/apphost/AndroidManifest.xml), whose build script compiles this same res dir.

     WHY THIS EXISTS (parity):
     The Activity's theme is not decoration — it is where Android resolves the default style of every
     widget the port constructs (editTextStyle, progressBarStyle, switchStyle, buttonStyle, ...), and so
     the field chrome, metrics and tints the port renders with. Getting it wrong shifts every
     field-bearing page by a few pixels. With NO android:theme at all, targetSdk 34 applies
     Theme.DeviceDefault (Material You), whose ?android:colorBackground is the Material3 tonal surface —
     a purple-tinted white (measured #F1F0F7 on the maui-test emulator) that the parity review flagged as
     "port page background is light lavender-gray vs MAUI's white".

     WHAT THIS IS: a REPRODUCTION OF MAUI'S OWN THEME, item for item, from the oracle at
     src/Core/src/Platform/Android/Resources/values/styles.xml (Maui.MainTheme.Base +
     Maui.MainTheme.NoActionBar + MauiMaterialButton + MauiCheckBox), with the brand colours replaced by
     the neutral native-default greys MauiReference pins in
     port/maui-reference/app/Platforms/Android/Resources/values/colors.xml (parity policy item 4 — the
     reference renders native-default controls, not the #512BD4 template brand).

     HISTORY (2026-07-26). This theme previously parented on
     @android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar and hard-pinned android:windowBackground /
     android:colorBackground to white, because the app hosts linked android.jar ONLY: there was no
     AppCompat/Material AAR on the classpath (no gradle), so the NoActionBar framework theme plus a white
     pin was the closest reachable approximation of MAUI's Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight.
     tools/parity/android-aar-lib.sh now links the real AndroidX + Material AARs out of the local NuGet
     cache, so the theme parents on the REAL Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight — exactly what
     Maui.MainTheme.Base parents on. Measured effect of the theme switch ALONE (no handler change) over a
     32-page regression sweep in both themes: 8 scores closer to MAUI (activity_indicator 1.32%->0.55%
     light and 1.47%->0.94% dark, date_picker 0.78%->0.57%, time_picker 0.71%->0.53%, picker
     0.79%->0.29%, switch dark 0.74%->0.51%, stepper 0.03%->0.00%, plus clip_views/pickers/progress_bar
     marginally), ZERO worse, the rest byte-identical.

     TWO THINGS THIS THEME MUST NOT DISTURB, both asserted programmatically by
     MauiHostActivity.onCreate: the #BDBDBD status bar (matching Maui.MainTheme's colorPrimaryDark) and
     the page surface (white light / #121212 dark). The old explicit white background pins are therefore
     gone — DayNight already resolves colorBackground the way MAUI does, and the Activity paints the
     window + content root authoritatively on top of it. -->
<resources>
    <!-- MauiReference's neutralized native-default palette (Platforms/Android/Resources/values/colors.xml):
         the dotnet-new-maui template's #512BD4 brand purple neutralized to platform grey, so accent-tinted
         DEFAULTS fall back to the native look. Explicitly-colored demo controls are unaffected. -->
    <color name="mauiColorPrimary">#E0E0E0</color>
    <color name="mauiColorPrimaryDark">#BDBDBD</color>
    <color name="mauiColorAccent">#E0E0E0</color>

    <style name="MauiAppHost.Theme" parent="Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight">
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/mauiColorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/mauiColorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/mauiColorAccent</item>
        <item name="materialButtonStyle">@style/MauiMaterialButton</item>
        <item name="checkboxStyle">@style/MauiCheckBox</item>
        <item name="android:textAllCaps">false</item>
        <!-- Mirrors MAUI's own theme, src/Core/src/Platform/Android/Resources/values/styles.xml:18-19.
             Both keys are needed: `alertDialogTheme` is what an AppCompat AlertDialog.Builder reads, and
             `materialAlertDialogTheme` is what MaterialAlertDialogBuilder reads — the picker's dialog goes
             through the latter, but a Builder constructed without an explicit theme falls back to the
             former, so setting only one leaves a path on framework chrome. -->
        <item name="alertDialogTheme">@style/MauiAlertDialogTheme</item>
        <item name="materialAlertDialogTheme">@style/MauiAlertDialogTheme</item>
        <!-- Maui.MainTheme.NoActionBar. MAUI's Android gallery renders these native-default ContentPages
             with NO top app-title bar, and app_host.cpp's content_chrome_height_px reserves no action-bar
             height — it subtracts only the status bar (top) and navigation bar (bottom). -->
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Byte-for-byte MAUI's own, src/Core/src/Platform/Android/Resources/values/styles.xml:83-85. The
         colorPrimary override is what makes the dialog's title and its Cancel button read as onSurface
         rather than the app accent — without it the Material dialog is the right SHAPE but the wrong
         colour, which on this board's neutralised #E0E0E0 palette would be an obvious miss. -->
    <style name="MauiAlertDialogTheme" parent="ThemeOverlay.MaterialComponents.MaterialAlertDialog">
        <item name="colorPrimary">?attr/colorOnSurface</item>
    </style>

    <style name="MauiMaterialButton" parent="Widget.MaterialComponents.Button.UnelevatedButton">
        <!-- MAUI manages min size, padding and insets itself; zero all of them, as Maui.MainTheme does. -->
        <item name="android:minWidth">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:minHeight">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:paddingLeft">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:paddingRight">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:paddingTop">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:paddingBottom">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:insetTop">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:insetBottom">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:insetLeft">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:insetRight">0dp</item>
    </style>

    <style name="MauiCheckBox" parent="Widget.Material3.CompoundButton.CheckBox">
        <item name="android:minWidth">0dp</item>
        <item name="android:minHeight">0dp</item>
        <item name="buttonTint">?attr/colorPrimary</item>
    </style>
</resources>
